# fixtures/iword-goto/goto.steps -- the REAL WordPerfect 5.1 (03-09-92) under
# DOSBox-X, driven by ../wordperfect51-decomp/tools/mint_drive.sh (bead
# initech-1zk9): PgUp / PgDn (Reference p. 104 "First Line on the Next /
# Previous Page") and Go To (Ctrl-Home; Reference p. 223-224) on a document
# of two hard pages, one more page and a soft page after 54 lines.
# Minted 2026-10-23 on a scratch copy of ../wordperfect51-decomp mint/work
# (the corpus untouched); each `shot NAME` is NAME.png beside this file.
# The preamble's first Return went INTO the document: line 1 is blank, so
# "Page one line two." is Ln 1.33"; page 3 is "Page three." + 53 blank lines
# and the 54th Return starts the soft page 4. Read: 03-06 PgDn (next page's
# first line at the screen top, Pos 1"; on the last page the document's
# end), 07/12 PgUp, 10 the column not kept, 13/14/22 "Go to " + digits,
# 15/16/17/23/29 Enter (page; past the end the last; 0 page 1), 18/19
# Esc/F1 cancel, 20/21 Backspace + Enter with no digits: no move, 25/26 Go
# To Up/Down, 27 Go To w, 28 Go To twice, 30 "Go to 2x" (a letter echoed;
# its Enter not minted). Graded by test_iword_face.c leg F16.
sleep 7
key Return
sleep 4
type Page one line one.
key Return
type Page one line two.
key ctrl+Return
type Page two line one.
key Return
type Page two second line here.
key ctrl+Return
type Page three.
key Return
